# Frontend

## Stack
Next.js (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, React Query. No math, aggregations, or financial projections in the UI — display API results only.

## Layout
- `app/` — pages and layouts (App Router)
- `components/` — UI only
- `lib/` — API clients, React Query setup, shared types aligned with backend Pydantic contracts

## API contracts
Call FastAPI through typed clients in `lib/`. Types must match backend schemas. Do not invent extra DTO fields on the client.

## React Query
- Use QueryClient from `lib/` (single provider in the root layout)
- Server state: `useQuery` / `useMutation` only — no ad-hoc `fetch` in components for domain data
- Cache keys must be stable and descriptive (e.g. `["dashboard"]`, `["bill", id]`)
- Mutations invalidate related queries after success
- Handle loading and error states in the UI; do not swallow failures

## Tailwind CSS
- Style with Tailwind utility classes; avoid new global CSS except `globals.css` tokens
- Prefer composition in `components/` over one-off page markup duplication
- Keep the dashboard readable: savings, charts, and an "ESG Eligibility Status" badge from API flags — do not compute eligibility in React
